1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,432
It's three in the morning

2
00:00:01,527 --> 00:00:03,146
in an emergency room

3
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:04,364
A doctor is meeting a woman

4
00:00:04,384 --> 00:00:06,382
with cancer for the first time

5
00:00:06,402 --> 00:00:07,900
And nobody in that room

6
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:09,700
knows what she wants

7
00:00:09,759 --> 00:00:11,739
So her family has to have the hardest

8
00:00:11,759 --> 00:00:13,650
conversation of their lives

9
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:15,146
all over again

10
00:00:16,009 --> 00:00:17,739
In India, ninety-eight percent

11
00:00:17,759 --> 00:00:18,918
of people with advanced

12
00:00:18,938 --> 00:00:20,275
cancer don't get the

13
00:00:20,295 --> 00:00:22,075
palliative care they need

14
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:24,039
Yes, you heard that right

15
00:00:24,491 --> 00:00:25,521
Ninety-eight

16
00:00:26,009 --> 00:00:27,700
That's why we built Sahara

17
00:00:27,956 --> 00:00:29,561
It's an app for people with cancer

18
00:00:29,581 --> 00:00:32,364
and for the families who look after them

19
00:00:32,384 --> 00:00:33,257
We're five people who

20
00:00:33,277 --> 00:00:34,754
met at Health-a-thon

21
00:00:35,134 --> 00:00:36,971
Basith and Awaiz run a software

22
00:00:36,991 --> 00:00:38,843
company called WeDevIT

23
00:00:39,402 --> 00:00:42,968
Dr Sujay is from IISc, Bengaluru

24
00:00:43,402 --> 00:00:46,396
Dr Sharada is from AIIMS, Mangalagiri

25
00:00:46,545 --> 00:00:47,900
And Shirin is a final-year

26
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,218
medical student

27
00:00:49,259 --> 00:00:50,525
Back in August, we had

28
00:00:50,545 --> 00:00:51,986
our first team meeting

29
00:00:52,170 --> 00:00:53,686
And Dr Sujay told us something

30
00:00:53,706 --> 00:00:55,504
that stayed with all of us

31
00:00:55,831 --> 00:00:56,739
Patients do tell you what

32
00:00:56,759 --> 00:00:58,504
they want at the end of life

33
00:00:58,563 --> 00:01:00,311
But nobody writes it down

34
00:01:00,331 --> 00:01:03,611
And in an emergency, nobody can find it

35
00:01:03,938 --> 00:01:05,989
So we did what technical people do

36
00:01:06,009 --> 00:01:07,361
We built everything

37
00:01:07,474 --> 00:01:10,004
Screen after screen, all for doctors

38
00:01:10,402 --> 00:01:12,932
Then we asked ourselves one question

39
00:01:13,152 --> 00:01:15,221
Why would a family install all this?

40
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:17,043
So we pivoted, towards the

41
00:01:17,063 --> 00:01:19,057
patient and the family

42
00:01:19,813 --> 00:01:22,096
And we kept one thing at the centre

43
00:01:22,116 --> 00:01:23,825
the goals of care talk

44
00:01:24,152 --> 00:01:25,436
That's when the doctor

45
00:01:25,456 --> 00:01:27,293
the patient and the family sit

46
00:01:27,313 --> 00:01:28,846
down together, and decide

47
00:01:28,866 --> 00:01:30,968
what kind of care she wants

48
00:01:31,081 --> 00:01:32,596
With everyone's consent

49
00:01:32,616 --> 00:01:34,646
the doctor records that talk

50
00:01:35,027 --> 00:01:37,218
AI writes out who said what

51
00:01:37,313 --> 00:01:40,611
For Indian languages, we use Sarvam AI

52
00:01:40,724 --> 00:01:42,204
Then the AI checks that

53
00:01:42,224 --> 00:01:44,146
nothing important was missed

54
00:01:44,188 --> 00:01:45,650
It goes through thirteen topics

55
00:01:45,670 --> 00:01:46,918
taken from India's

56
00:01:46,938 --> 00:01:48,186
end-of-life care guidelines

57
00:01:48,206 --> 00:01:49,846
written by the national critical

58
00:01:49,866 --> 00:01:52,521
care and palliative care societies

59
00:01:53,295 --> 00:01:55,168
Then the AI turns the conversation

60
00:01:55,188 --> 00:01:57,664
into a goals of care document

61
00:01:57,688 --> 00:01:59,932
That's a clinical record of her wishes

62
00:02:00,063 --> 00:02:01,432
Does she want CPR?

63
00:02:01,706 --> 00:02:02,829
A ventilator?

64
00:02:02,849 --> 00:02:04,182
Intensive care?

65
00:02:04,206 --> 00:02:06,504
And where does she want to be cared for?

66
00:02:06,866 --> 00:02:08,614
Nothing is final until the doctor

67
00:02:08,634 --> 00:02:11,829
reads it, corrects it, and signs it

68
00:02:11,849 --> 00:02:13,775
Then the family signs too

69
00:02:13,795 --> 00:02:15,057
and it's locked

70
00:02:15,759 --> 00:02:17,436
We also took legal advice on the

71
00:02:17,456 --> 00:02:19,900
wording and the format of that document

72
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:22,629
But goals of care is only the start

73
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:24,471
Sahara stays with the family

74
00:02:24,491 --> 00:02:26,521
every single day

75
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:28,486
Patients track their symptoms

76
00:02:28,563 --> 00:02:29,561
They rate how they're feeling

77
00:02:29,581 --> 00:02:31,132
on a distress thermometer

78
00:02:31,152 --> 00:02:32,114
and they mark where it

79
00:02:32,134 --> 00:02:33,718
hurts on a body map

80
00:02:34,081 --> 00:02:35,114
Their doctor can see how

81
00:02:35,134 --> 00:02:36,789
it's changing over time

82
00:02:37,027 --> 00:02:38,364
There's a mood journal, for the days

83
00:02:38,384 --> 00:02:40,200
that are hard to put into words

84
00:02:40,349 --> 00:02:41,632
They take a photo of a prescription

85
00:02:41,652 --> 00:02:43,593
or a medicine strip

86
00:02:44,116 --> 00:02:45,239
AI works out the medicines

87
00:02:45,259 --> 00:02:47,914
and reminds them about every dose

88
00:02:48,099 --> 00:02:49,257
They upload their reports

89
00:02:49,277 --> 00:02:52,164
and ask a question in plain words

90
00:02:52,474 --> 00:02:54,829
AI answers, and shows the exact

91
00:02:54,849 --> 00:02:56,846
line in the report it came from

92
00:02:56,866 --> 00:02:58,507
Their next hospital visit is

93
00:02:58,527 --> 00:03:00,307
scheduled right in the app

94
00:03:01,045 --> 00:03:02,329
Family members get their own login

95
00:03:02,349 --> 00:03:04,754
so everyone stays in the loop

96
00:03:04,991 --> 00:03:07,471
There's an emergency SOS button

97
00:03:07,491 --> 00:03:10,025
And a QR card that carries the patient's

98
00:03:10,045 --> 00:03:12,611
wishes, contacts and medicines

99
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:14,793
We also scraped public listings

100
00:03:14,813 --> 00:03:16,436
and put over sixteen hundred

101
00:03:16,456 --> 00:03:17,686
palliative care centres

102
00:03:17,706 --> 00:03:20,468
from across India, on one map

103
00:03:20,599 --> 00:03:23,650
It even shows where to find oral morphine

104
00:03:23,670 --> 00:03:25,043
And there's a community

105
00:03:25,063 --> 00:03:27,521
so no family goes through this alone

106
00:03:27,902 --> 00:03:30,346
Families don't talk in just one language

107
00:03:30,366 --> 00:03:31,632
So Sahara understands

108
00:03:31,652 --> 00:03:34,343
English, Hindi, Telugu

109
00:03:34,509 --> 00:03:36,650
Urdu and Kannada, even when

110
00:03:36,670 --> 00:03:38,557
they're mixed in one sentence

111
00:03:38,616 --> 00:03:40,757
Now, back to that emergency room

112
00:03:40,777 --> 00:03:42,775
One scan of her QR card, and the

113
00:03:42,795 --> 00:03:45,254
doctor knows exactly what she wanted

114
00:03:45,474 --> 00:03:47,900
Oh, wait. Late one night

115
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:49,132
something hit us

116
00:03:49,152 --> 00:03:51,361
We kept asking how the patient feels

117
00:03:51,491 --> 00:03:53,132
Nobody was asking her daughter

118
00:03:53,152 --> 00:03:55,087
So caregivers get their own wellbeing

119
00:03:55,107 --> 00:03:57,879
check too, and someone to call

120
00:03:58,384 --> 00:04:00,632
All of this took three months

121
00:04:00,652 --> 00:04:03,025
We had a lot of meetings with our doctors

122
00:04:03,045 --> 00:04:05,061
We met our mentor for a review

123
00:04:05,081 --> 00:04:06,454
And we ran a survey of

124
00:04:06,474 --> 00:04:08,132
doctors and hospitals

125
00:04:08,152 --> 00:04:09,686
We saved our work to GitHub

126
00:04:09,706 --> 00:04:11,843
almost six hundred times

127
00:04:12,045 --> 00:04:14,111
Each of those is called a commit

128
00:04:14,402 --> 00:04:16,521
It's one more improvement to the app

129
00:04:16,581 --> 00:04:17,507
It's built with free

130
00:04:17,527 --> 00:04:19,007
and open-source tools

131
00:04:19,027 --> 00:04:21,164
and it runs on a cloud server

132
00:04:21,402 --> 00:04:23,043
When Sahara got shortlisted

133
00:04:23,063 --> 00:04:25,775
we rebuilt it as a full Android app

134
00:04:25,795 --> 00:04:28,629
And it's live on Google Play today

135
00:04:29,134 --> 00:04:31,186
Sahara. Care that follows

136
00:04:31,206 --> 00:04:32,968
what matters to the patient

